## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Code Quality Anti-Patterns
- Manual error handling instead of helper functions
- Inconsistent response formats
- No performance monitoring
- Manual input validation
- No caching strategy
- Over-engineering simple components
- Under-testing critical paths

### ❌ Architecture Anti-Patterns
- Complex state management for simple data
- Microservices for monolithic application
- Advanced caching for small datasets
- Complex authentication for simple use case
- Over-optimization of simple queries

## Remember: Maintain consistent patterns, use helper functions, and focus on the actual requirements rather than theoretical perfection.